---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Asian side afternoon: Üsküdar, Çamlıca & Beykoz · HeyaGuide"
  description="A half-day route on the Asian side of Istanbul — Üsküdar tea, the giant Çamlıca Mosque, and the Bosphorus-village palaces of Beykoz. The Istanbul that most tourists miss."
>
  <article class="trip">
    <div class="trip-hero">
      <img src="/trips/asian-side-hero.jpg" alt="Çamlıca Mosque on the Asian side" />
    </div>

    <header class="trip-head container">
      <p class="trip-eyebrow">Day trip from Heya</p>
      <h1>Asian side afternoon: Üsküdar, Çamlıca & Beykoz</h1>
      <p class="trip-lede">
        Most visitors stay on the European side of Istanbul and never
        realise the Asian side is just as much the city — and quieter,
        and more local, and with a different set of sights. This
        half-day route threads three of the best of them: a working
        imperial mosque, the largest mosque in Turkey, and a
        waterfront palace built as a single-day rest stop for the
        sultan.
      </p>
      <div class="trip-meta">
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">From Heya</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">~50 min to Üsküdar</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">Total time</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">5–6 hours</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">Best for</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">An afternoon (12pm–6pm)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="trip-body container">
      <p class="trip-lede-2">
        The Asian side is the Istanbul that lives there — quieter
        neighbourhoods, water-front tea gardens, a mosque that the
        whole district organises around, and a string of imperial
        palaces along the upper Bosphorus that most visitors never
        reach. This route gives you a taste of three of them in one
        afternoon.
      </p>

      <h2>From Heya to Üsküdar</h2>
      <p>
        Take the F1 funicular to Taksim, then the M2 metro one stop to
        Şişhane, then change to the M2 (going the other direction)
        to Yenikapı, then change to the Marmaray to Üsküdar. Or
        simpler: F1 to Taksim, walk to the T2 funicular, take it down
        to Kabataş, then a 15-minute ferry to Üsküdar.
      </p>
      <p>
        Actually the simplest is just F1 + walk to Kabataş, then the
        15-minute ferry to Üsküdar — and the ferry is part of the
        experience, threading past the Maiden's Tower and the entire
        Asian waterfront on the way in. Total from Heya: about
        35–45 minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>Stop 1: Üsküdar and Şemsi Pasha Mosque (1 hour)</h2>
      <p>
        Üsküdar is one of the oldest continuously-inhabited parts of
        the city, and one of the most authentically Istanbul. Start
        with a tea at the pier of <a href="/places/semsi-pasha-mosque">Şemsi Pasha Mosque</a> — a tiny 16th-century mosque by
        Mimar Sinan, sitting on a pier over the Bosphorus, with the
        Maiden's Tower visible in the water just offshore. Order a
        çay (a few lira), find a bench, and watch the ferries.
      </p>
      <p>
        From the pier, walk 5 minutes uphill to the much larger
        <a href="/places/yeni-valide-mosque">Yeni Valide Mosque</a> on
        the hill above — an imperial mosque, big courtyard, classic
        Ottoman proportions. The interior is calmer than the Blue
        Mosque or Süleymaniye (less touristed, more working mosque).
        From the courtyard wall, you can see the Bosphorus and the
        European side.
      </p>

      <h2>Stop 2: Çamlıca Mosque (1 hour)</h2>
      <p>
        From Üsküdar, take the M5 metro 3 stops to Çamlıca (about
        10 minutes) and walk 5 minutes to the
        <a href="/places/camlica-mosque">Büyük Çamlıca Camii</a> — the
        largest mosque in Turkey, opened in 2019. It can hold 63,000
        worshippers (8,500 inside the main hall, another 35,000 in the
        surrounding courtyards), and it's a modern take on classic
        Sinan-era architecture: one massive central dome, six pencil
        minarets, pale marble and soft blue tilework.
      </p>
      <p>
        You don't need to be Muslim to enter — visitors are welcome
        outside prayer times. Modest dress (covered shoulders, knees);
        scarves and abayas are available at the visitor entrance. Give
        yourself 30–40 minutes inside, then walk 10 minutes up the hill
        to <a href="/places/camlica-hill">Çamlıca Hill</a> for a tea
        with the best view in the city.
      </p>

      <h2>Stop 3: Küçüksu Palace (1 hour)</h2>
      <p>
        Back down to Çamlıca metro, then continue north on the M5
        two more stops to Üsküdar (yes, you come back through Üsküdar
        — the M5 is a U-shape). From Üsküdar, take a taxi or local
        bus 15A up the Asian Bosphorus coast to
        <a href="/places/kucuksu-palace">Küçüksu Palace</a>, a small
        rococo mansion built in 1856 as a one-day rest stop for the
        sultan on his Bosphorus cruises.
      </p>
      <p>
        Küçüksu is small but extraordinary: gilt-trimmed ceilings,
        Bohemian-crystal chandeliers, a private marble bath carved
        from a single block, and a water-gate opening directly onto
        the Bosphorus where the imperial caiques used to tie up.
        Allow 30–45 minutes. The tea garden in the back garden is
        nice for a quick stop before heading back.
      </p>

      <h2>Stop 4 (optional): Hidiv Pavilion (30 minutes)</h2>
      <p>
        If you have energy left, the
        <a href="/places/hidiv-kasri">Hidiv Kasrı</a> is 3 km further
        up the Bosphorus from Küçüksu — a 1907 Art Nouveau mansion
        built for the khedive of Egypt, in a forest above the water.
        The interior is a small museum; the real reason to come is
        the hilltop park with panoramic Bosphorus views. Skip this
        if you're tired; otherwise it's a 10-minute taxi north.
      </p>

      <h2>Returning to Heya</h2>
      <p>
        The fastest return is M5 from Üsküdar to Ünalan, then M2
        back to Şişhane-Mecidiyeköy, then a short walk to Taksim
        and the F1 funicular down to Heya. Total: about 50 minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alternative: take the ferry from Üsküdar back to Kabataş at
        sunset (15 minutes, ₺20 with Istanbulkart). The light on
        the Bosphorus is best at this hour, and you'll see the Maiden's
        Tower, the Bosphorus Bridge, and the European-side skyline
        from the water.
      </p>

      <h2>Practicalities</h2>
      <ul class="trip-practical">
        <li><strong>What to wear:</strong> for the mosques, modest dress (covered shoulders and knees; scarves and abayas are available at Çamlıca's visitor entrance). For everything else, whatever's comfortable.</li>
        <li><strong>What to bring:</strong> Istanbulkart with ~₺100 on it (you'll use it for the metro, the ferry, and possibly the bus). Sunscreen and water in summer.</li>
        <li><strong>Friday prayer time:</strong> Çamlıca and Yeni Valide close for ~30 min around the noon prayer on Fridays. Plan around it.</li>
        <li><strong>Combo with Kadıköy:</strong> if you have an extra evening, add the <a href="/places/kadikoy">Kadıköy</a> meyhane (tavern) dinner. Take the Marmaray one stop north from Üsküdar and you're there.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related places</h2>
      <ul class="trip-related">
        <li><a href="/places/semsi-pasha-mosque">Şemsi Pasha Mosque</a> — the tiny Sinan pier mosque</li>
        <li><a href="/places/yeni-valide-mosque">Yeni Valide Mosque</a> — the imperial mosque on the hill</li>
        <li><a href="/places/camlica-mosque">Büyük Çamlıca Camii</a> — Turkey's largest mosque</li>
        <li><a href="/places/camlica-hill">Çamlıca Hill</a> — the view above the mosque</li>
        <li><a href="/places/kucuksu-palace">Küçüksu Palace</a> — the small rococo palace</li>
        <li><a href="/places/hidiv-kasri">Hidiv Kasrı</a> — the Art Nouveau mansion (optional)</li>
        <li><a href="/places/kadikoy">Kadıköy</a> — for a meyhane dinner at the end of the day</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trip {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .trip-hero {
    aspect-ratio: 21/9;
    max-height: 420px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-muted);
  }

  .trip-hero img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .trip-head {
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--container-pad) var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .trip-eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
    color: var(--color-brand);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .trip-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trip-meta-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .trip-meta-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-meta-value {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-body {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--container-pad) var(--space-9);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-lede-2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .trip-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  .trip-body li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .trip-body a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
  }

  .trip-practical li {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .trip-practical strong,
  .trip-related strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-related {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-related li {
    padding: var(--space-2) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trip-related li:first-child,
  .trip-related li:nth-child(2) {
    border-top: none;
  }

  .trip-related a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .trip-hero {
      aspect-ratio: 4/3;
      max-height: 280px;
    }
    .trip-related {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
